I just spent the last day and a half arguing with a Symbios=20
53c810 controller over whether it was going to work with kernel=20
2.4.  I went through 2.4.19, 2.4.18, 2.4.16, and Debian's=20
patched 2.4.18, all with no luck (though the thing works just=20
fine under Debian's 2.2.20).  Gathering debug messages points to=20
SCSI bus timeouts.

Now, just for kicks, I threw in a QLogic 1040 controller to see=20
how it would respond.  It appears to do much the same=20
thing--works under 2.2.20, but doesn't work on any of the 2.4=20
kernels I've tried.  I don't know how to get extra-verbose debug=20
messages out of this driver, but I assume it's the same=20
problem--which suggests that SCSI is broken on these 2.4 kernels=20
and the Alpha.

So what I'd like to know now is, has anyone had better luck than=20
I have, or am I just stuck with kernel 2.2 for now?

For those who'd like to know, the box is a PC164LX motherboard,=20
600MHz 21164 CPU, 512MB PC100, S3 Trio64, Intel PRO/100 NIC, and=20
the two SCSI cards I mentioned above.

On a side note, how is DMA-enabled performance of the CMD646=20
controller on this motherboard?  Comparable to Intel PIIX4, or=20
something rather less spectacular?

