Hi Tom,

There hasn't been as much work on the Alpha port of OOo as i386, ppc or
s390 and there is a lot that still needs to be done.  Gwenole Beauchesne of
Mandrake has been working on the port recently, although I don't know how
far he has got.  There were several 64 bit issues, and the highly
hand-optimised 'bridges' project needs to be ported for the architecture+ABI
combination too.  The dev@porting.openoffice.org mailing list archives can
tell you more, and is a good place to ask questions / get involved in
testing the port:

http://porting.openoffice.org/servlets/ProjectMailingListList

For more information about the porting process and what is needed, have a
look at the documents that are linked from this page:

http://porting.openoffice.org

And, don't forget OOo in Debian: debian-openoffice@lists.debian.org :)

Chris

