Sigh... :-\

I was hoping for a TGA2, but what you've got is one of the Intergraph
boards that we (DEC/COMPAQ/HP) OEMed from them.

They also had a Cirrus VGA for text mode console support, AND occupied
two (2) PCI slots, as you can see, the second slot for the accelerator
(better than both having to go through a bridge, IMHO).

Nice cards, so I'm told, but there are no free X servers that support
them, AFAIK. And almost certainly not even any commercial ones that'll
run under Alpha Linux.

Best option is to replace it with something known to work well with
the older Alphas, such as Matrox Millenniums or some of the ATI Mach64s.
The ATI Rage128 and the original ATI Radeon work on there quite nicely,
and will do 3D with the appropriate XFree86 (4.1.0 or later). The later
Radeons may be more of a problem, though the 7000 (VE) ought to be OK,
but I don't know about the 7500 or 9000 PCI versions...

Good luck.

